1
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:12,267
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,233
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:43,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:46,467
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:56,600
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,967 --> 00:00:59,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:00,967
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:02,267
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,367 --> 00:01:03,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,967
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:13,033
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,133
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,233 --> 00:01:19,167
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:22,100
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:25,167
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:28,200
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:31,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:36,133
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:37,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:38,967
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,067 --> 00:01:41,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:48,133
<i> Welcome back, Gabo.</i>

24
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,733
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

25
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:52,200
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GROANS]

26
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:55,867
<i>You thought I was going
to forget about it?</i>

27
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:58,700
<i>I got imprisoned for eight
years because of you!</i>

28
00:01:58,833 --> 00:01:59,867
<i> You'll pay for all of it!</i>

29
00:02:00,033 --> 00:02:03,367
- [GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

30
00:02:03,533 --> 00:02:06,333
<i>Django was beaten
to a pulp by Gabo!</i>

31
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:10,033
<i>That means, Gabo is the new
king of Ginintuang Lupa!</i>

32
00:02:10,167 --> 00:02:12,367
<i>This won't be the last
you'll see me, Gabo.</i>

33
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:13,700
<i> To the new king!</i>

34
00:02:13,867 --> 00:02:16,100
<i>- Long live Gabo!
- Long live!</i>

35
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:18,500
<i> I'll send you to your grave!</i>

36
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:20,533
<i>You promised you'd change
for the better, didn't you?!</i>

37
00:02:20,633 --> 00:02:21,833
<i> What if they killed you?!</i>

38
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:24,033
<i>I promised myself
that when I get out,</i>

39
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:27,367
<i>I'll make him feel all
the suffering I went through!</i>

40
00:02:27,467 --> 00:02:29,233
<i>Don't waste your time
getting revenge</i>

41
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:31,233
<i>at those
good-for-nothing pricks!</i>

42
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,067
<i>Listen to me. I just want
you to have a decent life.</i>

43
00:02:34,233 --> 00:02:37,333
<i>I'm sorry for letting my
emotions get the best of me.</i>

44
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:40,267
<i>I promise I'll try my best
to change.</i>

45
00:02:40,433 --> 00:02:41,600
<i>I'll avoid getting
into any trouble.</i>

46
00:02:41,767 --> 00:02:45,100
<i>Your Aunt Pinky has this piece
of property she's selling.</i>

47
00:02:45,267 --> 00:02:46,367
<i> We bought it.</i>

48
00:02:46,467 --> 00:02:47,933
<i> It's in Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

49
00:02:48,133 --> 00:02:49,367
<i>But there are many families
living there.</i>

50
00:02:49,467 --> 00:02:51,200
<i>And that area's known
for crime.</i>

51
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,200
<i>They'll just move
to the hills or somewhere.</i>

52
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,767
<i>They always find
a place to stay.</i>

53
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:57,100
<i>But, Mom, we can't just
let them be.</i>

54
00:02:57,233 --> 00:02:58,800
<i>Many families
will be left homeless.</i>

55
00:02:58,967 --> 00:03:00,033
<i> Let's put it this way.</i>

56
00:03:00,133 --> 00:03:02,233
<i>They've been staying at
Ginintuang Lupa for years.</i>

57
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:04,433
<i> So, as the new owners,</i>

58
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,433
<i>it's our turn to make use
of that property.</i>

59
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,033
<i>I told Papa during our talk
that I'll turn over a new leaf.</i>

60
00:03:10,133 --> 00:03:12,733
<i>So tomorrow,
I'll look for a job.</i>

61
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:17,567
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

62
00:03:17,667 --> 00:03:22,267
I'm glad that you and Gabo
had a serious talk.

63
00:03:23,133 --> 00:03:26,000
I really hope
he fulfills his promise.

64
00:03:26,167 --> 00:03:30,800
Well, I know that Gabo
has a good heart.

65
00:03:30,967 --> 00:03:32,967
It's just that he grew up
in a tough environment.

66
00:03:33,133 --> 00:03:34,100
We can't change that now.

67
00:03:34,267 --> 00:03:36,567
People here are taught that
if you don't fight back,

68
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:37,800
you'll be
at a disadvantage.

69
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,767
I really hope he changes
for the better.

70
00:03:39,933 --> 00:03:41,733
He'll end up living
a messy life

71
00:03:41,867 --> 00:03:45,400
if he keeps getting
into trouble.

72
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:49,167
Why don't we just
let him be?

73
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:52,067
He was imprisoned
for eight years.

74
00:03:52,167 --> 00:03:54,900
Maybe he learned
something there.

75
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:58,033
I mean, he wouldn't be
released on parole

76
00:03:58,167 --> 00:04:00,533
if he hadn't done something
good there.

77
00:04:00,667 --> 00:04:01,533
That's right.

78
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:04,500
You know, I'm proud
of my son.

79
00:04:04,633 --> 00:04:07,667
He can just be short-tempered
sometimes.

80
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:11,033
Maybe once he has a
family and job...

81
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:12,767
he'll change.

82
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:15,433
I guess when he gets older...

83
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:20,333
he'll realize the things he
needs to change.

84
00:04:20,467 --> 00:04:21,933
I hope so. I really do.

85
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:23,933
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:04:24,033 --> 00:04:26,267
Morning! Excuse me.
I'm coming through.

87
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,200
Move. Make some way.

88
00:04:28,367 --> 00:04:29,800
Good morning!

89
00:04:31,233 --> 00:04:32,200
[TEKLA] Hey.

90
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,500
- Mister Elton.
- Oh. Tekla.

91
00:04:35,667 --> 00:04:38,900
- Wow! Nice outfits.
- I know, right? How do we look?

92
00:04:39,033 --> 00:04:42,133
You're really serious
about looking for a job.

93
00:04:42,233 --> 00:04:44,567
- Finally tired of being bums?
- You're so harsh.

94
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:48,533
Well, it's high time
you help your parents out

95
00:04:48,667 --> 00:04:51,800
and stop loafing around
in the streets.

96
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:52,967
I hate his tone!

97
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:57,633
That's why we're going
job hunting with Gabo.

98
00:04:57,767 --> 00:05:00,000
Look, job hunting is easy.

99
00:05:00,167 --> 00:05:02,467
The question is
whether we'll be hired.

100
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,067
I mean, look at us.

101
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,833
We didn't even finish
elementary school.

102
00:05:05,933 --> 00:05:08,600
[TEKLA LAUGHING]
Well, excuse me, Bong.

103
00:05:08,733 --> 00:05:11,267
Don't lump me in with you.
Because look at me.

104
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,600
With how pretty and sexy I am,

105
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:15,400
you think no one
would hire me?

106
00:05:15,533 --> 00:05:17,433
I'm sure you'll be hired.

107
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:19,700
- With your beauty...
- Oh, thank you.

108
00:05:19,867 --> 00:05:21,500
- and your fair skin...
- Right?

109
00:05:21,633 --> 00:05:23,267
- Try a beerhouse.
- [BONG, IPE CACKLING]

110
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,833
- Like your grandmother.
- You're so mean!

111
00:05:25,933 --> 00:05:29,033
I have bigger dreams, you know!
And with this beautiful face?

112
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:33,233
I should be working
at a hotel or an office! Right?

113
00:05:33,367 --> 00:05:35,933
Wait, do you even know
how to speak English?

114
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:38,600
Nope!
But that doesn't matter.

115
00:05:38,733 --> 00:05:40,700
It's all about looks nowadays.

116
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,867
- She has a point.
- Hmph! They're such killjoys.

117
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,867
- [DANTE LAUGHING]
- Bye, Mister Dante!

118
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,567
[TEKLA] Anyone home?

119
00:05:46,733 --> 00:05:48,300
- Come in!
- Good morning!

120
00:05:48,433 --> 00:05:49,633
- Hey!
- Where's Gabo?

121
00:05:49,767 --> 00:05:51,067
- Join us for breakfast.
- Breakfast?

122
00:05:51,233 --> 00:05:53,867
- Yes! Join us.
- Perfect! We haven't eaten.

123
00:05:53,967 --> 00:05:55,800
- [BETCHAY CHUCKLES]
- Wow.

124
00:05:55,933 --> 00:05:57,933
That looks delicious!

125
00:05:58,067 --> 00:06:00,033
But it's only for us.

126
00:06:00,133 --> 00:06:01,733
Oh, come on.

127
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:05,300
They're going job hunting.
Of course, they'll need energy.

128
00:06:05,433 --> 00:06:06,967
So, they have to eat.

129
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,133
Miss Mameng is right,
Miss Betchay.

130
00:06:13,133 --> 00:06:14,400
Just get one, okay?

131
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:16,967
- Okay.
- Thanks.

132
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:19,267
You know what? I'm on a diet.
Just take my share.

133
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:21,633
- You're such a killjoy.
- What?

134
00:06:21,767 --> 00:06:22,733
But don't worry.

135
00:06:22,867 --> 00:06:26,067
Everything you gave us?
Put it all on our tab.

136
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:29,633
We'll pay for it once we receive
our first salaries.

137
00:06:29,767 --> 00:06:31,233
I hope so!

138
00:06:31,333 --> 00:06:32,833
- Where is Gabo?
- [BETCHAY] Oh.

139
00:06:32,967 --> 00:06:39,900
[THRILLING ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]

140
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:51,033
If I get heads,
I'll surely get a job.

141
00:06:52,133 --> 00:06:56,600
But if I get tails, that means
I'm down on my luck.

142
00:06:56,700 --> 00:07:03,167
[THRILLING ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

143
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:05,467
Ooh! Heads!

144
00:07:06,233 --> 00:07:08,967
It means I'm going
to land a job. [CHUCKLES]

145
00:07:09,633 --> 00:07:12,100
[SMOOCHES]
Looks like it's my lucky day.

146
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,767
[BETCHAY] Gabo!

147
00:07:17,333 --> 00:07:20,400
- Wow! So handsome!
- Look at you!

148
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:23,300
- [LAUGHTER]
- We're job hunting, right?

149
00:07:23,433 --> 00:07:26,167
You look like you're auditioning
for reality TV!

150
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:28,133
[RUDY]
Son, sit down and eat first.

151
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:30,533
- [MAMENG] Yeah.
- Thanks, Pa.

152
00:07:30,667 --> 00:07:32,000
But we have to go.

153
00:07:32,167 --> 00:07:35,233
We need to be early
to beat all other job hunters.

154
00:07:35,933 --> 00:07:38,133
[MAMENG] Okay.
But, Gabo...

155
00:07:38,233 --> 00:07:42,233
Don't forget what you
and father talked about.

156
00:07:42,367 --> 00:07:45,567
And I hope this marks the start
of you reaching your dreams.

157
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:46,967
[BETCHAY] Of course!

158
00:07:47,067 --> 00:07:49,667
He's going to reach
all of his dreams

159
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:52,533
as long as he works hard

160
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,500
and follows the right path.

161
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,600
Pa, we'll get going now.

162
00:07:58,733 --> 00:08:00,333
- Take care.
- Bye, auntie.

163
00:08:00,467 --> 00:08:02,400
- Be safe, okay?
- Excuse us.

164
00:08:02,533 --> 00:08:04,067
- Good luck!
- Thank you!

165
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,233
- We'll be off now.
- Bye, Miss Mameng.

166
00:08:06,367 --> 00:08:08,500
- Bye-bye!
- Take care!

167
00:08:08,633 --> 00:08:09,767
- Come on. Betchay.
- [IPE] Thank you!

168
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:12,333
The kid's trying to change.
When will you?

169
00:08:12,467 --> 00:08:13,667
- Huh?
- Excuse me.

170
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,667
Gabo! Gabo?

171
00:08:15,767 --> 00:08:17,333
Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!

172
00:08:17,433 --> 00:08:19,000
- Gabo!
- Pa?

173
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:20,067
Uh...

174
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:23,667
I really do hope you land a job

175
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,400
so you can truly change
for the better.

176
00:08:26,467 --> 00:08:27,733
Don't worry, Pa.

177
00:08:27,833 --> 00:08:31,067
I promise you we'll
come back here with jobs.

178
00:08:31,167 --> 00:08:32,600
Office workers, perhaps?

179
00:08:32,767 --> 00:08:34,733
- [LAUGHTER]
- I'll count on that!

180
00:08:34,833 --> 00:08:36,367
I mean, look at you!

181
00:08:36,467 --> 00:08:38,033
You all look like you're
going to the office!

182
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:40,533
- Or the bank!
- Yeah!

183
00:08:40,633 --> 00:08:43,033
- More like bank robbers!
- [LAUGHTER]

184
00:08:43,133 --> 00:08:45,233
Don't worry, Mister Rudy.
We got you.

185
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:48,400
Once we get our pay, we'll treat
you to a boodle fight!

186
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,933
Oh, I hope you make good
on your promise!

187
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,200
- Yeah.
- Go on now.

188
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:54,267
- Be careful.
- We'll get going now.

189
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:55,500
Take care, son.

190
00:08:55,667 --> 00:08:56,733
- Bye, Mister Dante.
- Bye.

191
00:08:56,833 --> 00:08:59,067
- Thanks, Mister Rudy.
- Mister Dante, don't jinx us!

192
00:08:59,167 --> 00:09:01,067
- Let's go.
- Come on!

193
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,100
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

194
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,967
I can already picture
the sparkling new...

195
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:12,800
...Ginintuang Lupa Beach Resort
Casino Hotel!

196
00:09:12,967 --> 00:09:15,933
After that, I'll buy you
all the cars you want.

197
00:09:16,033 --> 00:09:19,833
Oh, you know, I have
this special car in mind.

198
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,133
Which one?

199
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:24,467
I want one with
the matching umbrella!

200
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:26,933
I know a contractor who has one.

201
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:29,467
Uh, boss? The cars are ready.

202
00:09:29,633 --> 00:09:31,000
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

203
00:09:31,133 --> 00:09:33,333
- [ISOBEL] Oh, yes. Okay! Go!
- Good morning, ma'am.

204
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:35,000
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

205
00:09:35,133 --> 00:09:36,433
- Good morning...
- Hi, good morning!

206
00:09:36,533 --> 00:09:38,167
...my beautiful baby!

207
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,333
Leaving already?

208
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,967
Well, the investors
changed their minds.

209
00:09:42,067 --> 00:09:44,600
They want to see
the property today.

210
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,533
So, you'll be needing an escort?

211
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:48,600
- No, we can manage.
- [MAX] Are you sure?

212
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:49,767
I'm sure.

213
00:09:49,867 --> 00:09:51,667
Did you guys talk about
where the people

214
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,367
from Ginintuang Lupa
are going to move?

215
00:09:53,533 --> 00:09:57,333
We don't need to discuss it.
Just do your job.

216
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:01,433
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

217
00:10:01,567 --> 00:10:02,900
Take care.

218
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:05,567
- Bye, Mom.
- Yeah.

219
00:10:08,933 --> 00:10:12,000
[BONG] Gabo, what kind of job
are we getting?

220
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:14,300
Whatever. Anything.

221
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,467
Hey!
We can work at a call center!

222
00:10:16,567 --> 00:10:18,100
Isn't that the trend now?

223
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,500
Us?! At a call center?!

224
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:23,000
You doubting us?
We can speak English, right?

225
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,400
[BONG] Yes, of course!

226
00:10:24,567 --> 00:10:26,367
The problem isn't English.

227
00:10:26,367 --> 00:10:29,133
The problem is,
how far did we get in school?

228
00:10:29,233 --> 00:10:33,700
Exactly. As far as I know,
we need a college degree.

229
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:35,633
- Is that so?
- You probably forgot.

230
00:10:35,767 --> 00:10:37,200
We only reached third grade.

231
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:42,033
Whoa, hold on! That's just you
three. Don't include me.

232
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:45,200
Excuse me.
I finished fifth grade.

233
00:10:45,367 --> 00:10:47,000
- Hello?
- [LAUGHS] Look at this girl.

234
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:49,700
Flexing like she's all that.

235
00:10:49,867 --> 00:10:53,333
Oh! This is perfect!
"Wanted: live seller"!

236
00:10:53,467 --> 00:10:54,400
What's a live seller?

237
00:10:54,533 --> 00:10:56,500
People who sell stuff
on their phones.

238
00:10:56,633 --> 00:10:57,767
You know, online.

239
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:02,400
Yeah, Gabo. We've seen those.
They're the hot, sexy girls.

240
00:11:02,533 --> 00:11:04,333
- Mm.
- So? Let's go for it!

241
00:11:04,433 --> 00:11:06,333
Come on, hurry!

242
00:11:06,467 --> 00:11:07,600
Hello, madam!

243
00:11:07,767 --> 00:11:09,867
- Hey! You look great in pink!
- Good day to you!

244
00:11:09,967 --> 00:11:11,067
What can I do for you?

245
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:13,467
Uh, we'd like to apply
for a job.

246
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:16,033
Oh, we don't have openings
for repackers anymore.

247
00:11:16,167 --> 00:11:18,467
You're so funny, madam!

248
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:22,200
Look at me. Do I look like
a repacker to you?

249
00:11:22,333 --> 00:11:24,900
Of course, we're applying
to be live sellers.

250
00:11:25,067 --> 00:11:26,800
You guys? Live selling?

251
00:11:26,933 --> 00:11:28,533
Do you even know
how to sell?

252
00:11:28,667 --> 00:11:29,600
- Ah...
- [IPE] Ah...

253
00:11:29,733 --> 00:11:31,933
- Yes, yes, yes!
- We know how.

254
00:11:32,067 --> 00:11:33,633
Yes! We do, madam!

255
00:11:33,767 --> 00:11:35,400
You know what,
just let us try it out

256
00:11:35,567 --> 00:11:37,700
so you can see
how good we are.

257
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,900
Alright, fine.
I'll give you a shot.

258
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,633
If you sell a lot today,
you're hired.

259
00:11:43,833 --> 00:11:46,167
Oh, madam, don't worry.

260
00:11:46,333 --> 00:11:48,667
We got this. We'll sell out
your stock today.

261
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:50,667
Hello! Hello! Hello!

262
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,167
<i> Good day to everyone!</i>

263
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:57,500
<i>I'm Tekla, the prettiest
live seller on Earth!</i>

264
00:11:57,633 --> 00:12:00,500
And we are here at the most
beautiful hardware store

265
00:12:00,667 --> 00:12:01,767
in the whole Philippines!

266
00:12:01,867 --> 00:12:07,233
<i>And the first thing we have
for you are nails! Whoo!</i>

267
00:12:07,367 --> 00:12:09,000
These nails are so strong.

268
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:11,300
<i> Stronger than relationships!</i>

269
00:12:11,433 --> 00:12:12,733
<i> So buy them now!</i>

270
00:12:12,867 --> 00:12:15,267
<i> They can handle any disaster.</i>

271
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:18,000
<i>They're stainless.
They won't rust</i>

272
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,633
through storms, floods,
earthquakes, anything!

273
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:23,100
Your grandkids will use them!

274
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,667
<i> They're really that good!</i>

275
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,933
<i>- So buy them now!
- Why is she like that?!</i>

276
00:12:27,067 --> 00:12:28,433
Seriously!

277
00:12:28,533 --> 00:12:30,467
- Like she doesn't know how!
- Great deal right here!

278
00:12:30,633 --> 00:12:32,033
<i> The viewers don't look happy.</i>

279
00:12:32,167 --> 00:12:34,200
Oh, I'm not for sale, sorry--

280
00:12:34,333 --> 00:12:37,100
Hey! What is this!
I thought you knew how?

281
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:40,600
We're just warming up.
Look, people are buying.

282
00:12:40,733 --> 00:12:43,267
- You'll ruin my business!
- We're just getting started.

283
00:12:43,367 --> 00:12:44,700
Maybe they want the drill.

284
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:47,267
- Yeah, let's do that.
- Maybe they haven't seen this.

285
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:49,600
This is a drill! Yes! For all...

286
00:12:49,733 --> 00:12:52,867
<i>of our friends out there,
this is a top-quality drill.</i>

287
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,167
- Are they doing this right?
- [BONG] It's a tool

288
00:12:54,333 --> 00:12:57,233
made to punch holes, perfect
for your no-good neighbors.

289
00:12:57,367 --> 00:12:58,800
- Look at that.
- Anyone who wants to buy,

290
00:12:58,933 --> 00:13:00,067
just comment "mine."

291
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:02,967
<i>It's cheap and durable,
but they don't seem to want it.</i>

292
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,400
Ipe, Ipe, you're up.

293
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:06,300
- Oh no, it's his turn now.
- This one...

294
00:13:06,433 --> 00:13:09,867
is a hacksaw. It cuts anything.
It can cut...

295
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,367
<i> steel, sheet metal, wood,</i>

296
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,833
even your water line.

297
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,133
<i> Huh? What do you mean ugly?!</i>

298
00:13:17,267 --> 00:13:19,467
- Gabo, your turn.
- [BONG] You can do it.

299
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:23,733
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

300
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:26,267
- Can he make a sale?
<i> - Hello, viewers!</i>

301
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,000
<i> Come buy!</i>

302
00:13:28,133 --> 00:13:30,500
We have a hammer for sale!

303
00:13:30,633 --> 00:13:33,267
It's tough enough
to smash your heads!

304
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,333
- [TEKLA] That's right!
- Comment "mine" now!

305
00:13:35,467 --> 00:13:40,167
This steel won't rust, even
if I smash it in your face.

306
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,433
- [LAUGHING]
- We'll lose money here.

307
00:13:42,567 --> 00:13:44,200
This is the worst.

308
00:13:45,267 --> 00:13:47,900
<i> What? We look like thugs?</i>

309
00:13:48,033 --> 00:13:49,567
<i>- Oh boy.
- [TEKLA GASPS]</i>

310
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,167
<i>- These viewers are crazy.
- You guys are too much!</i>

311
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:52,867
If you want, come down here!

312
00:13:53,033 --> 00:13:54,500
You sell, and I'll break
your head!

313
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,567
- Come here! You're so smug!
- What?! Huh?!

314
00:13:56,733 --> 00:13:58,300
- They don't know us!
- You're watching us,

315
00:13:58,433 --> 00:13:59,433
but you can't afford anything!

316
00:13:59,567 --> 00:14:00,767
You're so cocky just
because you're watching!

317
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:03,067
- Tough guys behind a screen!
- Come over here!

318
00:14:03,233 --> 00:14:04,533
I'll smash your face!

319
00:14:04,633 --> 00:14:06,367
- Huh?! Huh?!
- [OBJECTS CLATTERING]

320
00:14:06,467 --> 00:14:08,233
- [WOMAN] Hoy, stop it!
- [GLASS SHATTERS]

321
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:09,700
- Why did it end up like this?!
- Stop!

322
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:10,933
- You'll ruin our business!
- What are you doing?!

323
00:14:11,067 --> 00:14:12,867
Get out of here!
We're calling the cops!

324
00:14:12,967 --> 00:14:14,233
- Gabo, run!
- Don't ever show your faces!

325
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:16,300
- You guys are crazy!
- All of you, get out!

326
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:21,967
[SEBASTIAN] Sam.

327
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:24,933
We checked out the jewelry
stores in Chinatown.

328
00:14:25,833 --> 00:14:30,100
Some of them are selling
their goods at very low prices.

329
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:32,067
They're also supplying
online sellers.

330
00:14:32,167 --> 00:14:35,967
These shops are owned by a
foreign national named Mr. Chan.

331
00:14:37,467 --> 00:14:38,500
Mr. Chan?

332
00:14:39,967 --> 00:14:41,967
Ma'am, check this out.

333
00:14:42,967 --> 00:14:44,900
We did a background check
on Mr. Chan.

334
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:46,367
He's a foreign national.

335
00:14:46,367 --> 00:14:48,233
He's faced tax evasion
charges before,

336
00:14:48,333 --> 00:14:50,133
but he always gets away with it.

337
00:14:50,267 --> 00:14:51,433
Oh no.

338
00:14:52,133 --> 00:14:54,400
Looks like someone in the
government is backing him up.

339
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:59,167
Okay. Let's keep an eye
on Mr. Chan.

340
00:14:59,167 --> 00:15:01,733
Find every information
you can get on him.

341
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,267
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

342
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:05,100
- Let's go, boys.
- Let's go.

343
00:15:10,233 --> 00:15:11,767
[IPE] Miss Betchay is right.

344
00:15:12,633 --> 00:15:14,767
We'll have a hard time
finding work

345
00:15:14,867 --> 00:15:17,100
because we didn't finish school.

346
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,267
[TEKLA SIGHS DEEPLY]

347
00:15:18,367 --> 00:15:21,333
I don't get it. We all have
pleasing personalities.

348
00:15:21,333 --> 00:15:23,967
What pleasing personality
are you talking about?

349
00:15:24,067 --> 00:15:26,133
Didn't you just destroy
the live selling studio

350
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,100
that's why we got fired?!

351
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,767
Gabo, what do we do now?

352
00:15:29,867 --> 00:15:31,800
Should we just give up
on the job hunt?

353
00:15:31,967 --> 00:15:35,767
What do you think, Gabo?
Should we keep going?

354
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:38,500
Of course.
Why give up now?

355
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:43,900
I'm sure we can find plenty
of work here at the market.

356
00:15:44,067 --> 00:15:45,967
Miss Betchay's right again.

357
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:48,233
We'd really end up
working at the market.

358
00:15:48,367 --> 00:15:49,900
Don't be picky.

359
00:15:50,033 --> 00:15:52,700
What's important is that we find
decent jobs.

360
00:15:52,833 --> 00:15:54,533
Come on.
Let's keep looking.

361
00:15:54,667 --> 00:15:56,333
We could've profited
off my beauty earlier,

362
00:15:56,433 --> 00:15:58,300
but you just had
to get us all fired!

363
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:02,767
Over there!

364
00:16:02,767 --> 00:16:04,233
- They're hiring!
- "WANTED: DELIVERY MEN..."

365
00:16:04,367 --> 00:16:05,567
- Huh?
- Let's go!

366
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,233
See there?

367
00:16:07,367 --> 00:16:09,367
They're hiring delivery men
and a cashier.

368
00:16:09,567 --> 00:16:10,533
Perfect!

369
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,100
- Tekla.
- Yeah?

370
00:16:12,233 --> 00:16:14,500
Being a cashier would suit you.
You're such a slave for money.

371
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,200
[MOCKING LAUGH]
You think you're funny?

372
00:16:16,367 --> 00:16:18,200
With you, the store might end up
with more losses than gains.

373
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:19,200
Why?

374
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:21,267
Well, we all know
you have sticky fingers.

375
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:24,700
Excuse me?! For your
information, I've changed!

376
00:16:24,867 --> 00:16:26,600
I only steal money
from my grandma nowadays.

377
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,200
Excuse me.

378
00:16:29,367 --> 00:16:30,533
- Yes?
- We're here to inquire...

379
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:34,167
...if you're still looking
for delivery men and cashiers.

380
00:16:34,267 --> 00:16:36,500
Yes, why? You interested?

381
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,600
- [BONG] Yes.
- Well... yes.

382
00:16:38,733 --> 00:16:43,067
We're hoping to find
decent jobs, sir.

383
00:16:43,267 --> 00:16:45,100
We can do whatever you ask us.

384
00:16:46,133 --> 00:16:49,300
Okay, I have goods scheduled
to be delivered later.

385
00:16:49,567 --> 00:16:50,933
[TEKLA SQUEALS] Perfect!

386
00:16:51,067 --> 00:16:54,267
How about a cashier?
Have you found one yet?

387
00:16:54,933 --> 00:16:56,700
Ah. [CHUCKLES]

388
00:16:56,833 --> 00:16:58,700
You're perfect for the job.

389
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:01,100
- [TEKLA GIGGLES]
- You'll surely attract buyers!

390
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:04,133
You're right, sir.
You have a good eye.

391
00:17:04,267 --> 00:17:05,733
Alright, come on in.
I'll give you an orientation.

392
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:07,367
- Right now?!
- Let's go!

393
00:17:07,467 --> 00:17:08,567
- Orientation?
- I like it here already!

394
00:17:08,667 --> 00:17:10,567
[TEKLA] We're so lucky!

395
00:17:10,667 --> 00:17:13,067
This is where I stack
the bags of garlic and onions.

396
00:17:13,167 --> 00:17:15,667
Later, you'll deliver them
to resellers

397
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:19,333
and our partner restaurants.

398
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:20,800
You think you can do it?

399
00:17:20,933 --> 00:17:23,133
Of course, boss.
That's easy.

400
00:17:23,133 --> 00:17:24,933
[IPE] Piece of cake, boss.

401
00:17:25,033 --> 00:17:25,967
- Basic!
- [LAUGHTER]

402
00:17:25,967 --> 00:17:27,133
[BONG] Basic, indeed.

403
00:17:27,267 --> 00:17:29,433
But how much
are we going to make?

404
00:17:29,533 --> 00:17:30,800
Six hundred per day.

405
00:17:30,933 --> 00:17:32,267
- Alright.
- Wait, boss.

406
00:17:32,367 --> 00:17:35,333
What about me? How much
am I going to make?

407
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:38,833
You should pay me more.
I'll be handling your money.

408
00:17:38,967 --> 00:17:41,933
With your beauty,
you deserve 800 a day.

409
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:45,100
- [SQUEALS] Sounds good to me!
- That's a lot!

410
00:17:45,267 --> 00:17:47,600
Okay, you can start.

411
00:17:47,933 --> 00:17:49,300
For now, organize those sacks.

412
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:51,167
Later, I'll have you
deliver them.

413
00:17:51,333 --> 00:17:52,333
Okay.

414
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:54,633
As for you, dear,
I'll show you the counter.

415
00:17:54,733 --> 00:17:56,167
- Let's go.
- This way.

416
00:17:56,333 --> 00:17:57,500
Let's get started.

417
00:18:00,233 --> 00:18:01,867
- You see these?
- Yes, sir.

418
00:18:02,033 --> 00:18:03,800
Make sure these are correct.

419
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,667
Excuse me, here's your order.

420
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:09,533
[VENDOR] Put them down.

421
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,500
[IPE] Should we put them inside?

422
00:18:14,467 --> 00:18:15,467
Here you go.

423
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,500
[BONG] Make way!

424
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,267
Coming through!

425
00:18:20,367 --> 00:18:22,333
Excuse me, sir.
Here's your order.

426
00:18:23,333 --> 00:18:24,467
[GRUNTS]

427
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:27,500
- There's the garlic.
- And the onions.

428
00:18:31,433 --> 00:18:33,400
- Thank you.
- Thank you, sir.

429
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:36,000
Looks like you're
all hardworkers.

430
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:38,133
Oh, of course, boss.

431
00:18:38,233 --> 00:18:40,700
You know, we've been looking
for jobs all day.

432
00:18:40,833 --> 00:18:42,133
Good thing you were hiring.

433
00:18:42,233 --> 00:18:45,667
As long as you work hard,
we won't have any problems.

434
00:18:45,933 --> 00:18:48,533
Especially you.

435
00:18:51,067 --> 00:18:53,467
- Do you have a boyfriend?
- [CHUCKLES]

436
00:18:53,567 --> 00:18:55,067
I do.

437
00:18:55,267 --> 00:18:56,900
I already have a boyfriend.

438
00:18:57,067 --> 00:18:59,200
It's Gabo, one of the
workers you hired.

439
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:03,900
If you haven't heard,
he just got out of jail.

440
00:19:04,067 --> 00:19:06,367
He served eight years.

441
00:19:06,467 --> 00:19:09,367
You see, the last time someone
tried to take advantage of me,

442
00:19:09,467 --> 00:19:11,733
he ended up with murder charges.

443
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,367
[NERVOUS CHUCKLE]

444
00:19:13,467 --> 00:19:15,400
O-Okay, just make sure
everything's in order.

445
00:19:15,567 --> 00:19:18,100
- Check our balances.
- Sure thing.

446
00:19:18,867 --> 00:19:20,900
See if everything's
accounted for, okay?

447
00:19:21,033 --> 00:19:22,833
You can count on me.

448
00:19:22,967 --> 00:19:26,833
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

449
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:30,467
What a dirty old geezer.

450
00:19:31,633 --> 00:19:33,600
I'm already taken. [CHUCKLES]

451
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:39,233
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

452
00:19:39,333 --> 00:19:42,467
[WOMAN] I'll buy one half kilo.
How much is it?

453
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:48,433
Psst.

454
00:19:52,667 --> 00:19:53,767
[WOMAN] Here's my payment.

455
00:19:56,133 --> 00:19:58,100
Tolits will approach that
woman with money.

456
00:20:04,333 --> 00:20:07,300
Miss, have it weighed again
just to make sure.

457
00:20:07,433 --> 00:20:11,300
There are vendors here
who scam buyers.

458
00:20:11,467 --> 00:20:14,467
Check the scale carefully.
It's all good, right?

459
00:20:14,633 --> 00:20:15,933
Alright then.

460
00:20:16,967 --> 00:20:18,467
- Hey! That's my wallet!
- Huh?

461
00:20:18,633 --> 00:20:20,933
- Thief!
- Go, go, go!

462
00:20:21,033 --> 00:20:24,133
- Run!
- Help! Thief!

463
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:27,633
[WOMAN] Thief! Thief!

464
00:20:27,767 --> 00:20:29,400
Move! Out of the way!

465
00:20:30,433 --> 00:20:31,467
Ow!

466
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:32,600
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

467
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:34,500
Hey!

468
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:39,367
- Ow!
- Ow! Stupid!

469
00:20:39,533 --> 00:20:42,300
- Gabo! Gabo!
- Get up!

470
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:44,333
What did you do
this time?

471
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:46,700
- Nothing.
- We didn't do anything.

472
00:20:46,867 --> 00:20:48,667
[GABO] Miss, what happened?

473
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:50,367
They took my wallet.

474
00:20:50,533 --> 00:20:53,333
You're stealing from people here
at the market now, huh?

475
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,000
- Have you no shame?
- Who took it?

476
00:20:55,133 --> 00:20:57,600
- I don't have it. I swear.
- Who took it?

477
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:59,633
- [BLOW LANDS]
- Ow!

478
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:03,000
- I don't have it, Gabo.
- Now, you.

479
00:21:03,133 --> 00:21:04,600
- I don't have it, Gabo.
- Who took it?

480
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:06,800
- I didn't steal anything.
- [BLOW LANDS]

481
00:21:08,567 --> 00:21:10,167
[IPE] Come on, stop lying.

482
00:21:10,733 --> 00:21:13,033
Who took it?
You still won't tell the truth?

483
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,400
